t{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\,{\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\text{ and }\\,{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}((2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}3{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{2}\\theta +\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546946 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547071 1069 "q-134557" 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547071 1071 "$5\\sqrt[3]{7}+3\\sqrt[3]{7}=$" 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547071 1072 #uuid "ea5d88b4-44af-57bd-9e77-32e6ed1711e4" 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547071 1074 "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{7}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt[3]{7}+3\\sqrt[3]{7} & = \\\\ (5+3)\\sqrt[3]{7} & = \\\\ 8\\sqrt[3]{7} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547072 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546931 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547072 1069 "q-67795" 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547072 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535947 17592186045417 true] [17592186547072 1071 "![](images/16/160b4